10
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
Mystify: Michael Hutchence is a 2019 documentary film about the life of musician, actor and
singer-songwriter Michael Hutchence, lead vocalist of the Australian rock band INXS.

11
01:02:20,000 --> 01:02:26,000
It is written and directed by Richard Lowenstein and relies primarily on rare archive footage, outtakes, private home
video and audio commentary provided by friends, ex-partners, band members, record producers and family.

12
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
An Australian-British venture, the film was co-produced by Ghost Pictures, Passion
Pictures with Madman Entertainment and Dogwoof serving as distributors.

13
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:46,000
It is in association with Baird Films and Film Victoria.

14
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
Mystify: Michael Hutchence had its world premiere at the Tribeca Film Festival on 25
April 2019, and was theatrically released in Australia on 4 July 2019.

15
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The film was released in the United Kingdom on 18 October
receiving generally positive reviews from critics.

16
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:46,000
The film explores themes of depression, suicide, rock
star, home video, archive footage.

17
01:36:20,000 --> 01:36:26,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
